# Argus GCS — environment variables
# Copy to .env next to run.py and uncomment/modify as needed. run.py loads it at
# startup, and the Vite dev proxy follows ARGUS_PORT from it. Variables already set
# in the shell win, and --host/--port win over both.
# The Windows package starts backend/server.py and does not read this file.

# ARGUS_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ARGUS_PORT=8100

# Replaces the default list, so keep any default origin you still use. Pages opened
# from another machine need their origin here, for example http://192.168.1.5:8100.
# ARGUS_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:8100,http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://127.0.0.1:8100

# ARGUS_NO_BROWSER=1

# Turns on authentication. The web UI asks for this token and remembers it.
# GCS_AUTH_TOKEN=your-secret-token-here

# A key of your own from console.tianditu.gov.cn turns the Tianditu map source on.
# ARGUS_TIANDITU_KEY=
